<section id="process" class="wrap pt0">
  <div class="sec-head rv">
    <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
    <h2>A clear process, from first call to scaling</h2>
    <p>I don't move live budget in week one. Tracking and structure get fixed first, or you end up optimising toward numbers that were never accurate.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="phases six stg">
    <div class="ph"><span class="when">Step 1</span><h3>Discovery</h3><p>I learn your offer, margins, sales process and what a customer is worth. Then I agree the single metric the account will be judged on.</p></div>
    <div class="ph"><span class="when">Step 2</span><h3>Account analysis</h3><p>A full review of your existing Google Ads account: wasted spend, structure, tracking accuracy and the opportunities already sitting in your search terms.</p></div>
    <div class="ph"><span class="when">Step 3</span><h3>Tracking &amp; build</h3><p>Conversion tracking verified end to end, campaigns restructured or rebuilt, audiences and exclusions configured, ad copy and assets prepared.</p></div>
    <div class="ph"><span class="when">Step 4</span><h3>Launch</h3><p>Changes go live in stages rather than all at once, so early data stays readable and I don't reset the learning period unnecessarily.</p></div>
    <div class="ph"><span class="when">Step 5</span><h3>Testing &amp; optimisation</h3><p>Weekly search term reviews, ad copy tests, bid strategy adjustments and landing page experiments, each documented.</p></div>
    <div class="ph"><span class="when">Step 6</span><h3>Reporting &amp; scaling</h3><p>Regular reporting against the agreed KPI, a monthly review call, and budget increases only where the numbers support them.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

